he higher bill they said that the company that sold them this debt was Phoenix Financial Services. I made a report on that company as well for purchasing false debt and trying to collect it.","8":"I have been called four times in  two  hours just today  XXXX / XXXX /  XXXX   alone. The company that has called me repeatedly is Phoenix financial services.","9":"Medical treatment received from an automobile accident. The 3rd party and XXXX accepted responsibility. The insurance company states this has been paid. After sending documentation numerous times and discussed on the phone, the debt collection agency continues to call, send mail and reports to the credit bureaus. I have had to send documentation to the credit bureaus to have this removed, sent documents to the medical facility, insurance company and debt collector with continued harassment.","10":"PHOENIX FINANCIAL SERVICES Date Opened : XX/2017 Account : XXXX Amount : {$420.00} Office of the CFO, Thank you for your recent inquiry. This is not a refusal to pay, but a notice that your claim is disputed. This is a request for validation made pursuant to the Fair Debt Collection Practices Act. Please complete and return the attached disclosure request form. Please be advised that I am not requesting a verification that you have my mailing address, I am requesting a validation : that is, competent evidence that I have some contractual obligation to pay you. Being that this was due to identity theft you are reporting negative information on my account that is not mine which is in direct violation of the FCRA section 605B. You should also be aware that sending unsubstantiated demands for payment through the United States Mail System might constitute mail fraud under federal and state law. Your failure to satisfy this request within the requirements of the Fair Debt Collection Practices Act will be construed as your absolute waiver of any and all claims against me, and your tacit agreement to compensate me for costs and attorneys fees. Lastly, I hereby withdraw any prior consent, either expressed or implied, for you to communicate with me in any form other than writing. In the event that you can not properly validate the debt, then you are demanded to cease and desist communication in all forms regarding this matter. Any communication from you and/or any agents, subsidiaries, etc., will be regarded as willful negligence along with any other applicable violation ( s ) and prosecuted to the full extent of the law if deemed necessary. Govern yourself accordingly. Sincerely, XXXX XXXX CREDITOR DISCLOSURE STATEMENT Name and Address of Collector ( assignee ) : Name and Address of Debtor : Account Number ( s ) : What are the terms of assignment for this account? You may attach a facsimile of any records relating to such terms. Have any insurance claims been made by any creditor been made by any creditor or assignee regarding this account? Yes /no Has the purported balance of this account been used in any tax deduction claim? Yes / no Please list the particular products or services sold by the collector to the debtor and the dollar amount of each : Upon failure or refusal of collector to validate this collection action, collector agrees to waive all claims against the debtor named herein and pay debtor for all costs and attorney fees involved in defending this collection action. X Authorized signature for Collector Date Please return this completed form and attach all assignment or other transfer agreements that would establish your right to collect this debt. Your claim can not be considered if any portion of this form is not completed and returned with the required documents. This is a request for validation made pursuant to the Fair Debt Collection Practices Act. If you do not respond as required by this law, your claim will not be considered and you may be liable for damages for continued collection efforts.","11":"Upon reviewing my credit report I noticed accounts from PHOENIX FINANCIAL SERVICES placed. I have never received any information written nor call about this alleged debt. I mailed validation letters twice via certified mail on XXXX XXXX 2017 and then again XXXX XXXX 2017. I am allowed under the Health Insurance Portability and Accountability Act ( HIPAA ) to protect my  privacy and medical records from third parties. I did NOT give permission to any of my current or prior medical providers to release any of my medical information to a third party. I am aware that the HIPAA does allow the release of limited information about me but anything more is to only be revealed with the patients authorization. Therefore, I asked them to allow me to validate this alleged debt and to send me detailed breakdown of fees and any collection costs and medical charges. I asked a for a copy of my signature with the provider of service to release my medicalinformation to PHOENIX FINANCIAL. I requested FULL documentation of what was received from  the provider of service. Lastly. I asked that they cease any credit bureau reporting until the debt has been validated by me. I also stated that if they can NOT provide ALL of this information they MUST remove this collection from my social and from all XXXX major credit bureaus such as XXXX, XXXX and XXXX. XXXX has NOT complied with my requests. Reporting and therefore continuing to report this invalid information to the credit bureaus and not allowing me to validate is a violation of the FCRA.","12":"I owe the amount of {$770.00} to XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX since XXXX XXXX, XXXX. Phoenix Financial Services LLC ( phoenixfinancialsvcs.com ), a Collections Agency, recently acquired this debt and they have done a Negative Re-Aging of this debt with all Credit Reporting agencies, by reporting it as a new debt in XXXX of XXXX. This is an illegal practice.","13":"Abusive, disrespectful, demeaning statements were made. I asked how we could settle the debt and the person stated, " what are you going to do - avoid us like the other 24 debts you have? ''","14":"I 've tried disputing a fraudulent collection account on my credit report. I 've sent letters to the agency an d have gotten little response. My official complaint is against PHOENIX FINANCIAL SE for reporting credit informati on to the credit reporting agencies that was a result of Identity Theft Ive asked in my letter that the negative reporting ceases and the information be removed from my credit report.","15":"Phoenix Financial Services just violated the Fair Debt Collection Practices Act and the Fair Credit Reporting Act by placing XXXX collections on my credit report that were previously deleted by another company and by not notifying me of these collection accounts. I only know they hit my credit report because I have credit monitoring and I got the alert today. They are reporting account number XXXX in the amount of {$570.00} and account number XXXX in the amount of {$1800.00}. Both of these accounts were deleted by XXXX XXXX over two months ago because they lacked proper validation on this account. And now XXXX is reporting an open date of XX/XX/2017 on my credit report which is so not true and false. I filed a complaint with the BBB and they told me that they sent their initial letter on XX/XX/2017 which is not true. I never received anything from them and they are lying. They have this on my credit report and it should not be on there.","16":"In my recent review of my credit report in XXXX XXXX, 2016. I see that Phoenix Financial Services reporting the same account to all XXXX credit reporting agencies. I request a total deletion under the FCRA. According to my understnading of the Fair Credit Reporting Act, their duty as creditors is to accurately report on all accounts and to correct any of all the mistakes as found by their accounting department or by myself as the consumer. I thank you in advance for upholding the federal law as directed by FCRA and removing this accounts immediately. 

